<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Benchmark and Baselines</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{E}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>E</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{E}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Rank</span> on the Massive Text Embedding Benchmark (MTEB) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Muennighoff et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. Specifically, we mainly evaluate its English v1 version, a collection of 56 datasets covering seven types of embedding tasks: classification, clustering, pairwise classification, reranking, retrieval, sentence similarity (STS), and summarization. We also leverage its English v2 version for quick evaluation and ablation studies, which is smaller and cleaner with 41 tasks. We compare our models with recent advanced open source text embedding models that are trained on public datasets, including Instructor-xl <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, BGE-large-en-v1.5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiao et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, GritLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Muennighoff et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, E5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, EchoEmbedding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Springer et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and LLM2Vec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">BehnamGhader et al., 2024</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Performance comparison on MTEB. Note that some baselines are trained with non-public data, and we only report the version trained on public data, marked using *. The best results for each subtask are highlighted in <span id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>, and the second-best results are <span id="S4.T4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_ulem_uline">u</span>nderlined.</figcaption>
