<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T4" title='Table 4 ‣ Benchmark and Baselines ‣ 4.3 Embedding Ability ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ "E"^2Rank: Your Text Embedding can Also be an Effective and Efficient Listwise Reranker' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> presents the performance of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{E}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>E</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{E}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Rank</span> on the MTEB(Eng, v1) benchmark. When leveraging only the public dataset, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{E}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>E</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{E}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Rank</span> demonstrates strong embedding capabilities, while <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{E}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>E</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{E}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Rank</span>-8B shows slight performance advantages on average compared to previous advanced models. Notably, compared with the variant with only contrastive learning, distilling from richer ranking signals will bring consistent and significant enhancements in retrieval tasks (<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow 1.58" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mn>1.58</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow 1.58</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{E}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>E</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{E}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Rank</span>-8B), demonstrating the effectiveness of the ranking objective. Noticed that here we focus on general and pure embedding ability, so we do not use the listwise prompt for reranking tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
